<Behavior #ai-data-workflow apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" (
  <Requirements [
    <Requirement #cybernetic-resource-agent-replanning (
      <Statement ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMB>
      A non-terminal AI Data run SHALL support a canonical graph patch that advances generation and re-executes an affected frozen resource Agent task until an unchanged verifier target is satisfied.
      </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMB>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #cybernetic-resource-agent-cases { name = "Cybernetic resource Agent replanning" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #observed-gap-before-replan (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMC>
              A frozen AI Data definition invokes a resource Agent and pauses at an observation boundary.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMC>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMD>
              The projected Agent output fails the run's immutable verifier.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMD>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RME>
              The failed observation SHALL be recorded before any graph mutation and the run SHALL remain non-terminal.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RME>
            )>
            <Case #canonical-patch-convergence (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMF>
              The controller has one structurally valid repair for the failed Agent node.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMF>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMG>
              It applies the repair through WorkflowApplyGraphPatch.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMG>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMH>
              The same run, definition and Agent identity SHALL advance to a new generation, invalidate affected facts, re-execute, and satisfy the unchanged verifier.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMH>
            )>
            <Case #adaptive-evidence-survives-recovery (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMJ>
              A patched Data run has converged at generation one.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMJ>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMK>
              Eidolon reloads the run from durable state.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMK>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMM>
              Patch history, invalidation facts, generation-aware Agent effects and Agent instance/session continuity SHALL remain observable.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMM>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
    <Requirement #autonomous-resource-agent-control-loop (
      <Statement ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMN>
      An autonomous AI Data run SHALL execute a resource-managed controller over one canonical checkpoint authority, admit only typed control decisions, and reuse exact Controller and Worker Agent instances across generations and recovery.
      </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMN>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #autonomous-resource-agent-control-cases { name = "Autonomous resource Agent control loop" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #protected-completion-barrier (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMP>
              A frozen autonomous AI Data definition identifies an immutable verifier and an explicit protected control node.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMP>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMQ>
              All ordinary graph nodes succeed but the current verifier has not produced PASS with an admitted complete decision.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMQ>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMR>
              The protected node SHALL remain waiting and the run SHALL remain non-terminal.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMR>
            )>
            <Case #atomic-admitted-transition (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMS>
              A Controller Agent proposes a decision against the current generation and the host admits it.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMS>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMT>
              The runtime commits that control iteration.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMT>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMV>
              Graph generation, control cursor, verifier report, feedback, admission and receipt SHALL become visible atomically in the same canonical checkpoint.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMV>
            )>
            <Case #frozen-dynamic-agent-proof (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMW>
              An admitted dynamic Agent node names an AgentDefinition and an exact frozen task proof.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMW>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMX>
              The node becomes ready.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMX>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMY>
              The runtime SHALL execute the frozen task binding only when workflow, node and AgentDefinition identities agree, otherwise fail before provider dispatch without mutating the graph.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMY>
            )>
            <Case #exact-instance-reuse (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMZ>
              A named Controller or Worker Agent has one durable instance binding in checkpoint profile state.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RMZ>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN0>
              A later iteration or recovered runtime invokes that logical Agent again.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN0>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN1>
              It SHALL target the exact reciprocal instance id and SHALL NOT create a replacement when the binding is missing, corrupt or inconsistent.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN1>
            )>
            <Case #bounded-invalid-decision-feedback (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN2>
              A Controller Agent emits an invalid, stale, duplicate or no-progress decision.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN2>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN3>
              The admission Processor rejects it.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN3>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN4>
              The runtime SHALL atomically record typed bounded feedback without changing graph generation, while propagating host invariant failures instead of treating them as model correction.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN4>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
    <Requirement #autonomous-planning-evidence (
      <Statement ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN5>
      Autonomous AI Data planning evidence SHALL bind proposition-neutral inputs to canonical multi-generation control facts, exact Agent identities and immutable verifier outcomes, while distinguishing deterministic mechanics from live-provider autonomy.
      </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN5>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #autonomous-planning-evidence-cases { name = "Autonomous planning evidence" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #two-distinct-observation-driven-patches (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN6>
              A proposition supplies only a goal, immutable verifier, frozen capability catalog, initial data and budgets.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN6>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN7>
              The autonomous control loop observes a first gap and a distinct verifier failure after its first admitted revision.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN7>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN8>
              It SHALL record two distinct admitted patch digests causally linked to those observations and converge without a harness-authored repair answer.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN8>
            )>
            <Case #invalid-decision-preserves-authority (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN9>
              A controller output is invalid and the current graph bytes and generation are known.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RN9>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNA>
              The output is normalized and rejected by admission.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNA>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNB>
              Typed bounded feedback SHALL be committed while graph bytes and generation remain unchanged.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNB>
            )>
            <Case #sealed-exact-reuse-evidence (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNC>
              A run is recovered after its first admitted patch and Agent invocations.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNC>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RND>
              The Controller and a repeated Worker are invoked in the fresh runtime.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RND>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNE>
              The sealed evidence SHALL prove targeted reuse of identical external instance and session identities and reject substitutions or fallback creation.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNE>
            )>
            <Case #evidence-class-separation (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNF>
              A deterministic provider double completes the same canonical runtime path as a live resource Agent.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNF>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNG>
              Its sealed receipt is evaluated for live-autonomy acceptance.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNG>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNH>
              The receipt SHALL be classified as mechanics-only and SHALL NOT satisfy a live-provider evidence gate.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNH>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
    <Requirement #live-autonomous-planning-convergence (
      <Statement ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNJ>
      A live-provider autonomous AI Data run SHALL let a resource Controller plan only from goal, frozen catalog and canonical observations, and SHALL preserve exact Controller/Worker identities while converging through admitted graph generations.
      </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNJ>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #live-autonomous-planning-cases { name = "Live autonomous planning convergence" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #live-outcome-driven-construction (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNK>
              A real provider receives a goal and frozen capabilities but no expected patch or verifier answer.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNK>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNM>
              The initial graph has no implementation path.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNM>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNN>
              The Controller SHALL emit an admitted revision, execute a resource Worker and complete only after the immutable host verifier passes.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNN>
            )>
            <Case #live-verifier-driven-second-patch (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNP>
              The first live generation is structurally valid but fails the unchanged verifier.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNP>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNQ>
              The failure facts are observed after fresh-runtime recovery.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNQ>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNR>
              The same Controller SHALL produce a distinct second admitted patch and the repeated Worker SHALL use the same external instance and session.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNR>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
    <Requirement #autonomous-agent-definition-preparation (
      <Statement ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNS>
      An AI Data Mission preparation step SHALL autonomously select or author a Halfcode AIAgentDefinition from typed task requirements, freeze it as a run-local fixed capability, and reuse the existing durable Agent instance runtime across graph generations and fresh recovery.
      </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNS>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #preparation-and-recovery { name = "Agent definition preparation and recovery" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #typed-preparation-before-run (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNT>
              A Mission goal requires a Worker contract but does not prescribe an AgentDefinition identity.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNT>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNV>
              The resource-managed Mission Controller prepares the AI Data run.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNV>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNW>
              It SHALL use typed candidate selection or author-new admission before freezing one fixed Agent capability for the run, without mutating a dynamic Capability Catalog.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNW>
            )>
            <Case #receipt-based-fresh-recovery (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNX>
              A preparation receipt was persisted with exact resource, proof and instance identities.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNX>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNY>
              A fresh runtime reconstructs the workflow.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNY>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNZ>
              It SHALL re-project the same resource closure, reproduce the same proof fingerprint and target the reciprocal durable instance id, otherwise fail without replacement creation.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RNZ>
            )>
            <Case #definition-instance-separation (
              <Given ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RP0>
              A selected or newly authored definition has an authentic task proof.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RP0>
              <When ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RP1>
              The Worker is invoked for the first and later graph generations.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RP1>
              <Then ?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RP2>
              Definition authoring and selection SHALL remain distinct from instance creation and by-id targeting, which continue through the generic Agent runtime.
              </?01M1A0DRN0Y2FKAGTSP9B55RP2>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
  ]>
)>
